kind i-want-to
title I want to see whether an install replaced a vtium.conf that I can put back.
intro The Flow tab's o lists the vtium.conf files that installs replaced. On a machine whose first install wrote vtium.conf, no install has replaced one yet.
see install-and-restore/put-back-the-vtium-conf-from-before-an-install
waits-for audit 5: "vtium-config has not installed anything yet" after it has

# No vtium.conf is installed yet: the first install writes it.
file etc/batch.conf
    ROOT/fonts/mono.bdf
font fonts/mono.bdf 8x16
draft
    version = 1
    [head console]
    vt = 5

1. Run `vtium-config install`.
2. Go to the Flow tab.
3. Press o to restore.
at the list
check screen lacks "has not installed anything yet"
4. Press Esc.
